<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Largs</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1263">1263</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scottish-norwegian-war">Scottish–Norwegian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Largs was fought on 2 October 1263 on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayrshire">Ayrshire</a> coast between Scots and part of the Norwegian fleet of King Haakon IV, which had been battered by storms. The clash itself was indecisive, but Haakon withdrew and died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkney">Orkney</a> that winter. His successor Magnus VI then negotiated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-perth">Treaty of Perth</a> of 1266, ceding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrides">Hebrides</a> and Man to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-largs.jpg" alt="Battle of Largs" width="320" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William Hole · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Largs_(detail),_1263.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
